                <pb facs="0215" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg113"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/417.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Hill to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-11-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>German Government agrees to postponement of the opium conference to February 1
                    next.</p>
                <p>Herr Roessler, consul at Canton and first German commissioner, has been given
                    rank and character of consul general for the period of the conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
